{"school":{"dbn":"20K259","name":"J.H.S. 259 William Mckinley","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"20","district_label":"District 20","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":1798,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"7305 FT HAMILTON PARKWAY, BROOKLYN, NY 11228","phone":null,"website":"www.McKinley259.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/67088","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"McKinley offers something for everyone: rigorous academics, arts, sports, and social-emotional supports. We offer gifted and honors programs through our screened program for Independent Investigation Method (IIM). McKinley has been an A-rated, Well-Developed school for many years, a Recognition school for the last two, but now we are a Local Support and Improvement School- formerly referred to as Good Standing. Parents are always welcomed at McKinley. Our Parent Teacher Association (PTA) meetings are often themed and actively involve parents and their children. Information is always made public through our Grades, Sttendance, and Messaging Application (GAM), our website, emails, and telephone. Interpreters are always available. We offer laptops, Interactive Boards, and wireless internet. Our murals has been featured on ABC, CBS, Channel 25, and The New York Times. We offer two state-of-the-art science labs and all students conduct hands-on science lab activities. We feature a business course called Virtual Enterprises Junior Ventures; in this course, students create their own product & market it for sale (similar to Shark Tank). We will also have 5 screened Independent Investigation Method (IIM) classes where students focus on learning research skills through project-based activities. We are a Community School and provide a College & Career course for all 7th grade students. Attending McKinley is an experience, not just a school with classes.","start_time":"08:35am","end_time":"0